{"full":"hf:build-small-hackathon/Scholar-Lens","spaceId":"build-small-hackathon/Scholar-Lens","name":"Scholar Lens","source":"huggingface","description":"An interactive AI application on Hugging Face Spaces.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["gradio","build-small-hackathon","backyard-ai","nvidia-nemotron","openai-codex","modal","literature-review","semantic-scholar","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":3,"created":"2026-06-07T07:13:28.000Z","updated":"2026-06-15T23:58:27.000Z","license":"mit","runtime":"SLEEPING","appUrl":"https://build-small-hackathon-scholar-lens.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/build-small-hackathon/Scholar-Lens","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T18:59:30.816Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T18:59:30.816Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T18:59:30.816Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🔬","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Scholar Lens is a small-model literature review assistant for atmospheric science. It searches scholarly sources, de-duplicates papers, maps paper relationships, and uses NVIDIA Llama-Nemotron-Nano 8B on Modal to write grounded, cited answers from retrieved abstracts.","The app is built for a real atmospheric-science literature review workflow: papers are scattered across databases, abstracts need to be compared quickly, and researchers need evidence-grounded synthesis rather than another list of links.","Scholar Lens keeps the model task focused: it retrieves paper metadata and abstracts first, then asks a small model to reason only over that context. If evidence is missing, the app is designed to say so instead of inventing sources."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/build-small-hackathon/Scholar-Lens/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"61eb50b3f745e0c9b6c8b3ca8ec8f8f730d358fef35dac25fb8c3ad4f916baf1","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T18:59:30.852Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T18:59:30.852Z","projectIn